# Social auth

- Client obtains an OIDC **id_token** (Google / Microsoft / Apple SDK). Backend does **not** run the browser redirect dance for APIs.
- Routes (enabled providers only):
  - `POST /api/v1/auth/social/google/`
  - `POST /api/v1/auth/social/microsoft/`
  - `POST /api/v1/auth/social/apple/`
  Body: `{ "id_token": "..." }`.
- After verify → get/create user + `SocialAccount` link → issue **JWT** or **session** (same mode as the rest of the project). Do not invent a parallel auth stack.
- Providers: Strategy via `SocialProvider` + `get_social_provider()`; configure env client IDs in `.env` / `config/settings/social_auth.py`.
- Require verified email on first link; Apple may omit email on later logins (must already have `SocialAccount`).
- Changing providers / routes / env → update **this rule file** + `auth` rule (+ `.env.example` / settings) in the **same** change.

